# Everything Scooplist needs. Set real values in the Vercel dashboard, never in a file.
#
# SCOOPLIST_PIN     The owner's PIN for the admin surfaces. Falls back to 7623
#                   (the Marshall shop phone's last four) so a demo works with
#                   zero setup — set a real one before this carries a real case.
# DATABASE_URL      Neon Postgres. One click in Vercel: project > Storage >
#                   Create Database > Neon, free tier. Without it the store
#                   falls back to in-memory and the admin says so plainly.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN
#                   Vercel Blob, for flavor photos. One click in Vercel:
#                   project > Storage > Create Blob store. Without it photos
#                   are stored inline in the database (fine for a demo, says
#                   so in the admin).
# SCOOPLIST_SECRET  Any long random string. Keys the HMAC in the admin cookie
#                   so cookie-guessing requires the secret, not just the PIN.
# SCOOPLIST_LOCATIONS
#                   The shops, as slug:Name pairs. Defaults to True North's two.
SCOOPLIST_PIN=
SCOOPLIST_SECRET=
DATABASE_URL=
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
SCOOPLIST_LOCATIONS=marshall:Marshall,battlecreek:Battle Creek
# SCOOPLIST_CATEGORIES
#                   The boards, as key:Label pairs. Defaults to ice cream
#                   (Hand-Scooped, Soft Serve, Dairy Free & Sorbet, Adult).
#                   A bar: taps:On Tap,cans:Cans & Bottles,na:Non-Alcoholic
# SCOOPLIST_ALLERGENS
#                   Comma list of allergen chips. Defaults to the ice cream
#                   four; set "-" for none (a tap list has no allergen chips).
# SCOOPLIST_SIZES   Default price lists per category key. Semicolon-separated
#                   blocks: taps=Half:$4|Pint:$7|Flight:$12;cans=Can:$5
#                   "-" = deliberately no default prices (the allergens
#                   convention): bare SCOOPLIST_SIZES=- for every category,
#                   or per category as taps=-. New flavors then start with
#                   an empty price list, and the library's "Another size"
#                   still prices a one-off. With SCOOPLIST_CATEGORIES set,
#                   an unpriced category never inherits the ice cream
#                   defaults either way — no invented prices on a bar.
# SCOOPLIST_EXAMPLE Example name in "new item" placeholders, so a bar is not
#                   prompted with ice cream. Defaults to Lemon Poppyseed.
SCOOPLIST_CATEGORIES=
SCOOPLIST_ALLERGENS=
SCOOPLIST_SIZES=
SCOOPLIST_EXAMPLE=
# SCOOPLIST_NOUNS   item,surface,prep - the vertical's own words for
#                   env-pinned installs (drink,cooler,in gives Cascarelli's
#                   its cooler). Store-configured installs get nouns from
#                   the /setup preset instead.
SCOOPLIST_NOUNS=
# SCOOPLIST_MASTER  Multi-org mode, the central deployment only. Setting this
#                   (with SCOOPLIST_LOCATIONS and SCOOPLIST_CATEGORIES both
#                   UNSET) flips the deployment to serving many organizations
#                   from one database: orgs are created with
#                   tools/create-org.mjs, owners sign in at /login/{org}, and
#                   sites read /api/v1/orgs/{org}/case/{location}. The value
#                   authorizes org creation, so it is a real secret: set it
#                   in the Vercel dashboard, long and random.
#                   THE TWO LIVE SINGLE-TENANT INSTALLS MUST NEVER SET THIS.
#                   Every other var above applies to legacy single-tenant
#                   deployments only; org config lives in the database. In
#                   org mode SCOOPLIST_SECRET still keys the session cookie
#                   and falls back to SCOOPLIST_MASTER when unset.
SCOOPLIST_MASTER=
